messages:
Jordan: heads-up — running into a weird module boundary error when importing @redwood/sdk from Next.js middleware (edge runtime). error is `Error: can't resolve 'fs'` during build even though i'm only using the hosted client in an edge function :thinking_face:

Priya: yup seen that. sdk's main export pulls in a node-only helper in the cjs entry. edge runtime bundlers (next/webpack/rspack) sometimes pick the wrong export. quick workaround is to import the edge-specific entry: `import { createClient } from '@redwood/sdk/edge'` if that exists, or dynamic import inside the handler:
```js
export default async function middleware(req) {
  const { createClient } = await import('@redwood/sdk/dist/edge');
  const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
  // ...
}
```

Eli: fwiw we hit a related typing issue — TS was pulling node types for Request/Response and complaining about missing `body` on the edge Request. adding "lib": ["dom", "es2020"] to tsconfig helped, or use the edge types override in the app's ambient d.ts.

Priya: another durable fix (we're prototyping) is to add an exports subpath for "/edge" in package.json so bundlers pick the tiny edge build. e.g.:
```json
"exports": {
  "./edge": "./dist/edge/index.mjs",
  "import": "./dist/esm/index.mjs",
  "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js"
}
```
This avoids the conditional export resolver getting confused by node-only deps.

Jordan: thanks — that helps. are there any known pitfalls with Next middleware specifically? iirc the edge runtime disallows certain globals and modules (crypto, fs, child_process) and also you can't use top-level await in pages/_middleware?

Eli: correct — crypto.webcrypto is fine but node's crypto isn't. also watch for packages that import 'stream' or 'fs/promises' even if you don't call those paths; bundlers can still include them unless you use an explicit edge entry. smaller tip: mark the file as middleware.ts in Next so it uses the edge runtime, and keep imports inside the function to ensure server-only cjs code isn't pulled into edge bundle.

Priya: opened a tracker item and example repo: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-edge-examples (WIP). devex note: we'll add an 'edge' export and a short section in the JS SDK readme about Next middleware gotchas and the TS lib settings. :memo:

devex-bot: created issue #412 on repo redwood-js-sdk: "Edge-friendly exports + README for Next middleware" (link above).
